Third-party material in tao-of-power

The MIT License in LICENSE covers the code and the original writing in this
repository (the English renderings, notes, questions, and other text written
for this project). The files below are not ours. They keep their own terms:

- Chinese text (Wang Bi edition), James Legge's 1891 translation, the Shuowen
  Jiezi, and the Mawangdui collation (sources/): public domain.
- Unihan data (sources/unihan.json and data built from it): Unicode License,
  https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
- Stroke data (app/data/strokes/): Make Me a Hanzi, derived from Arphic PL
  KaitiM, Arphic Public License.
- Pronunciation recordings (the syllable MP3 files in app/audio/): audio-cmn
  by Chen Wang, CC BY-SA.
- Passage recordings (app/audio/passages/): made with Google Cloud
  Text-to-Speech (WaveNet) from the public-domain Chinese text.
- Rare-character outlines (app/data/rare-glyphs.json): GlyphWiki.
- Search model (app/model/): Model2Vec potion-retrieval-32M by MinishLab,
  distilled from BAAI bge-base-en-v1.5, MIT License.
- Art (app/art/): public domain or CC0. Each work is credited in
  app/data/art.json.
- Fonts (app/fonts/): EB Garamond, Noto Serif TC, LXGW WenKai TC, SIL Open
  Font License.

R. L. Wing's The Tao of Power (1986) inspired this project. Its text is not
included here.
